== S3: universal quantifiers vs the active set
70:14. THE CI Pipeline SHALL rebuild every definition on a declared schedule at least once per day.
71:15. WHERE a declared publish policy is set to on-change THE CI Pipeline SHALL discard a scheduled rebuild whose canonicalised package set, taken as a sorted set of package type, name, version and package checksum per platform manifest, equals that recorded in the CycloneDX SBOMs attested to a published digest carrying its full release tag, pushing nothing, signing nothing and attesting nothing from it.
72:16. WHEN a scheduled rebuild produces an image whose resolved package set differs from that of a published digest carrying its full release tag, or for which no published digest carries that tag, THE CI Pipeline SHALL publish that image through criteria 2.7 to 2.9 and SHALL report in its job summary its package-set difference against any published digest carrying that tag.
57:1. WHEN a definition change merges to main THE CI Pipeline SHALL build affected images for every platform their definitions declare.
91:2. WHEN an upstream release matches a definition's version policy THE Renovate Automation SHALL open a pull request updating pinned ref, checksum, and derived tags.
92:3. WHEN multiple images share one upstream monorepo THE Renovate Automation SHALL group their bumps into a single pull request.
99:10. THE Scan Pipeline SHALL re-verify at least once per day each definition's declared authenticity signal against its upstream origin, and SHALL report each mismatch as a failure of that run and file an issue naming it as a supply-chain signal.
100:11. THE Renovate Automation SHALL track each upstream chart version pinned under chart/ against its chart repository and SHALL open a pull request, never automerged, for each new chart release matching its version policy.
126:2. WHEN a pull request affects an image or chart THE Test Suite SHALL install each affected chart on a kind cluster in CI.
43:13. THE Repository SHALL declare in its catalogue policy file an active set naming each definition it builds, tracks, tests and publishes.
44:14. THE CI Pipeline SHALL derive its build matrix, its chart and test matrices and its upstream tracking scope solely from that active set.
45:15. WHILE a definition sits outside that active set THE CI Pipeline SHALL publish no new digest for it.
46:16. IF a pull request bumps a definition outside that active set THEN THE CI Pipeline SHALL fail validation naming that definition.
47:17. THE Repository SHALL document per build archetype a builder contract naming its input, one definition directory, and its outputs, an image pushed by digest and per-platform SBOM material carrying package pull checksums.
109:1. WHERE an active definition declares an upstream chart THE Chart Adaptation SHALL consume that chart at a pinned version without modifying upstream templates.
129:5. WHEN pods are Ready THE Test Suite SHALL execute each active definition's declared functional probe.

